Each release gets a directory named after its version (X.Y.Z).
The directory name IS the version — no separate VERSION file needed.

releases/<version>/pre.sh   - install-check hook: runs in the OLD system before
                              any slot is written; non-zero exit aborts install.
releases/<version>/post.sh  - boot-slot post-install hook: runs in the OLD
                              system after slots are written, before reboot.
                              $RAUC_SLOT_MOUNT_POINT = new boot slot (mounted).
releases/<version>/notes.md - release notes for release.json.

Workflow:
  mkdir releases/1.0.2
  ./automation.sh build configs/prod-local --version 1.0.2
  ./automation.sh release prod --version 1.0.2

Run-once-with-this-update only. For run-every-update idempotent work use
overlay/usr/share/shareframe/system-migrations/ (executes in the NEW system).
